{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CJNCVyJBFm4Zm8rD61zZBZ","type":"tool_result","content":"=== files changed by 43eb34b ===\ncommit 43eb34bef2eecef3c28551f5f3088c1343aa06ff\nAuthor: mecattaf <thomas@mecattaf.dev>\nDate:   Sun Aug 30 05:12:39 2026 +0200\n\n    instruments: reconcile — the adapted instrument overlay is already in the lane\n    \n    Stateless reconcile attempt for revision 16ab40e1. The deliverable is present\n    and intact at the lane base (ff1731c); container/rootfs/fn_synctrace.py,\n    fn_offload_batch.py, fn_expert_union.py and tests/test_instruments.py are\n    byte-identical to their landing commit 4b1d714, which is an ancestor here.\n    \n    Verified against the task's goal, not just its acceptance command:\n    \n      - fn_synctrace.py wraps the seven Tensor methods that force a blocking D2H\n        (item/tolist/cpu/numpy/nonzero/__float__/__int__), one sys._getframe per\n        call, and carries upstream's bool-mask-indexing caveat verbatim. No env of\n        its own: install()/uninstall() bracket the FN_PROFILE window, matching the\n        reference's no-new-env-var discipline (ds4-vllm-manifest.md section 3.1).\n      - fn_offload_batch.py exposes resolve_store_batch_tokens and\n        resolve_promote_block_budget on FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC /\n        FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC, torch-free, with both load-bearing invariants\n        intact: the store floor at max(offloaded_block_sizes) and promotion\n        counted in blocks rather than tokens (section 3.3).\n      - fn_expert_union.py is re-targeted as the goal requires: it wraps\n        fused_topk in vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/\n        fused_topk_router.py, the choke point this workload actually routes\n        through, instead of upstream's gpt_oss_triton_kernels_moe\n        .make_routing_data, which is never on this model's path\n        (qsa-53896.md section 4). Kill switch FN_EXPERT_UNION defaults off;\n        FN_EU_START/FN_EU_CALLS/FN_EU_OUT shape the window.\n    \n    All three carry an \"Adapted from\" notice naming the upstream file, the\n    ds4-vllm revision a8f620d, and Apache License 2.0. The overlay is wired into\n    the image by container/Containerfile:117.\n    \n    Acceptance criteria pass unchanged (11 tests; 50 across the repo suite), so\n    this attempt makes no code change: re-authoring identical files would only\n    churn the history. Empty commit records the reconcile.\n\n=== all paths touched since base ff1731c ===","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed35101f-5870-4929-bc35-54b81f34c2c7","uuid":"3feb1b50-222b-418b-affb-a506694c0c22","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:17:00.196Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== files changed by 43eb34b ===\ncommit 43eb34bef2eecef3c28551f5f3088c1343aa06ff\nAuthor: mecattaf <thomas@mecattaf.dev>\nDate:   Sun Aug 30 05:12:39 2026 +0200\n\n    instruments: reconcile — the adapted instrument overlay is already in the lane\n    \n    Stateless reconcile attempt for revision 16ab40e1. The deliverable is present\n    and intact at the lane base (ff1731c); container/rootfs/fn_synctrace.py,\n    fn_offload_batch.py, fn_expert_union.py and tests/test_instruments.py are\n    byte-identical to their landing commit 4b1d714, which is an ancestor here.\n    \n    Verified against the task's goal, not just its acceptance command:\n    \n      - fn_synctrace.py wraps the seven Tensor methods that force a blocking D2H\n        (item/tolist/cpu/numpy/nonzero/__float__/__int__), one sys._getframe per\n        call, and carries upstream's bool-mask-indexing caveat verbatim. No env of\n        its own: install()/uninstall() bracket the FN_PROFILE window, matching the\n        reference's no-new-env-var discipline (ds4-vllm-manifest.md section 3.1).\n      - fn_offload_batch.py exposes resolve_store_batch_tokens and\n        resolve_promote_block_budget on FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC /\n        FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC, torch-free, with both load-bearing invariants\n        intact: the store floor at max(offloaded_block_sizes) and promotion\n        counted in blocks rather than tokens (section 3.3).\n      - fn_expert_union.py is re-targeted as the goal requires: it wraps\n        fused_topk in vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/\n        fused_topk_router.py, the choke point this workload actually routes\n        through, instead of upstream's gpt_oss_triton_kernels_moe\n        .make_routing_data, which is never on this model's path\n        (qsa-53896.md section 4). Kill switch FN_EXPERT_UNION defaults off;\n        FN_EU_START/FN_EU_CALLS/FN_EU_OUT shape the window.\n    \n    All three carry an \"Adapted from\" notice naming the upstream file, the\n    ds4-vllm revision a8f620d, and Apache License 2.0. The overlay is wired into\n    the image by container/Containerfile:117.\n    \n    Acceptance criteria pass unchanged (11 tests; 50 across the repo suite), so\n    this attempt makes no code change: re-authoring identical files would only\n    churn the history. Empty commit records the reconcile.\n\n=== all paths touched since base ff1731c ===","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
