{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeYD7w3z3B2dGDBQWWCsc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reconcile complete — the deliverable is already present, correct, and committed in the lane. No code change was warranted.\n\n**What I verified independently** (not taking the prior attempt's commit message at face value):\n\n- **`fn_synctrace.py`** — wraps the seven blocking-D2H `Tensor` methods (`item/tolist/cpu/numpy/nonzero/__float__/__int__`), one `sys._getframe(1)` per call (~25 events/step vs. the profiler's ~3,200), and carries upstream's bool-mask-indexing caveat. No env of its own; `install()`/`uninstall()` bracket the `FN_PROFILE` window, matching the reference's no-new-env-var discipline (`ds4-vllm-manifest.md` §3.1).\n- **`fn_offload_batch.py`** — torch-free (`import os` only), exposes `resolve_store_batch_tokens` / `resolve_promote_block_budget` on `FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC` / `FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC`, with both load-bearing invariants intact: store floor at `max(offloaded_block_sizes)` (`fn_offload_batch.py:160`) and promotion counted in **blocks**, not tokens (`fn_offload_batch.py:142`) — §3.3.\n- **`fn_expert_union.py`** — correctly **re-targeted** as the goal requires: it wraps `fused_topk` in `vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/fused_topk_router.py` (`fn_expert_union.py:125-152`), not upstream's `gpt_oss_triton_kernels_moe.make_routing_data`, which this workload never routes through (`qsa-53896.md` §4: `FusedMoEFactory → FusedTopKRouter → fused_topk`). `num_local_experts` comes off `gating_output.shape[-1]` (host metadata, no sync); slot-0 padding absorption keeps accumulation sync-free; `FN_EXPERT_UNION` defaults off and every failure path swallows.\n- All three carry an `Adapted from` notice naming the upstream file, revision `a8f620d`, and Apache License 2.0. The overlay is baked into the image by `container/Containerfile:117`.\n\n**Checks run:** the acceptance command passes (py_compile ×3, 3 notice headers, 11 tests); the whole repo suite is 50 tests, OK. `git status --porcelain` prints nothing.\n\n**Why no new commit:** the working tree is clean and HEAD (`43eb34b`) already records this task's reconcile on the assigned branch; the three modules and `tests/test_instruments.py` came in via ancestor `4b1d714`, below the lane base. Every path touched by a task commit stays inside `container/rootfs` and `tests`. Re-authoring byte-identical files, or stacking a second empty commit, would only churn history without changing the deliverable."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":356,"cache_read_input_tokens":63776,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":356},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed35101f-5870-4929-bc35-54b81f34c2c7","uuid":"d986f1c7-3afb-469a-bf5c-9276fa2ebbe5","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:18:34.222Z","request_id":"req_011CeYD7vJLQwsKeAkC58Njr"}
